{"at": "2026-11-06T08:03:15.627332+00:00", "event_id": "01M6QY491BBAZ9HKQD1RGY8X29", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M6QY46RJGFZN6WBVQQXCZSY6", "final_answer": "Unless the mission is specified with an explicit topology being defined, no worktrees/lanes/coord branch should be created. A single topic branch for the mission is minted, regardless of default branch protected status. Once the topology is settled, and the finalization has completed -> lanes/worktrees are created. That solves the discrepancy rather naturally, and is more efficient (delay creation until the topology is chosen). Rationale: reworking and reminting topologies is expensive, and compressing a lanes/coord topology into a single_branch one is the most expensive approach. The inverse is a lot simpler to perform.", "mission_id": "01M6QY1MKKW6AA3EBKSJ0VVAMP", "mission_slug": "lane-worktree-model-hardening-01M6QY1M", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": true, "rationale": "Operator ruling, stijn-dejongh, 2026-11-06 (epic #7276). Quoted as given.", "recorded_at": "2026-11-06T08:03:15.627332Z", "resolved_by": "stijn-dejongh", "run_id": "01M6QY46RJGFZN6WBVQQXCZSY6", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-06T08:03:15.625576Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
